# Configuring VLANs

## Objective
Implement Virtual LANs (VLANs) to segment network traffic in a network using a Cisco switch.

## Tools Used
- Cisco Packet Tracer
- Cisco Switch
- PCs
- Ethernet Cables

## Theory
A VLAN (Virtual Local Area Network) is used to logically divide a network into multiple broadcast domains. VLANs improve network security and reduce unnecessary traffic.

## Procedure

### Step 1: Enter Privileged Mode

Switch> enable


### Step 2: Enter Global Configuration Mode

Switch# configure terminal


### Step 3: Create VLANs

Switch(config)# vlan 10
Switch(config-vlan)# name SALES
Switch(config-vlan)# exit

Switch(config)# vlan 20
Switch(config-vlan)# name HR
Switch(config-vlan)# exit


### Step 4: Assign Ports to VLANs

Switch(config)# interface fastEthernet 0/1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if)# switchport access vlan 10
Switch(config-if)# exit

Switch(config)# interface fastEthernet 0/2
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if)# switchport access vlan 20
Switch(config-if)# exit


### Step 5: Verify VLAN Configuration

Switch# show vlan brief


## Result
VLANs were successfully created and ports were assigned to segment network traffic.
